<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="029" project="sdap-SPE-admin-app-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Surface billingClassification and billingStatus, warn when billing is invalid</title>
    <phase>3 Workstream C — Correct the API surface</phase>
    <gate>020 complete</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs (Graph read + DTO) and .tsx; tags include bff-api and frontend.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified read-only field exposure plus a warning state.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>medium</effort>
    <parallel-group>W10</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>020</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, frontend, fluent-ui</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Container types carry billingClassification and billingStatus. Invalid billing is a live operational failure mode with zero visibility today. Surface both and warn when billingStatus is not valid. This is READ-ONLY — attaching a billing profile belongs to provisioning, not this app.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the Graph container-type model and Fluent UI v9. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>Both fields render per container type, and a non-valid billingStatus produces a visible warning.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-C12 / §4.2d. Billing-profile ATTACH (Add-SPOContainerTypeBilling) is PowerShell, needs Azure subscription owner/contributor, and is a once-per-customer provisioning act — it belongs to customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1 and is out of scope here (task 062 raises it there). What SPE Admin does instead is read billing state and warn. Small, but genuinely missing.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Models/SpeAdmin/ContainerTypeDtos.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/SpeAdmin/ContainerTypeEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/SpeAdminApp/src/components/container-types</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">v1.0 endpoints — field names are v1.0 names.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: READ-ONLY. Do NOT implement billing-profile attach, change, or any billing write. That is provisioning's scope (spec §4.2d).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the warning. It MUST state what invalid billing means operationally and where to fix it — not merely display a red badge. Routing beats stonewalling.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: field names. Verify billingClassification and billingStatus against the current v1.0 schema before use.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06">Scope: these fields. If billing state is unavailable, show an explicit unknown state — never default to "valid".</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Scope: the warning UI. Fluent v9 semantic tokens; dark-mode correct; no hex literals.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this BFF change. Placement Justification in the PR; verify publish size.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Container-type billing fields</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>knowledge/sharepoint-embedded/docs/learn-containertypes.md</file>
      <file>projects/sdap-SPE-admin-app-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/sdap-SPE-admin-app-r2/notes/spe-platform-research-2026-08-20.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="endpoint-definition" location=".claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md">Minimal API endpoint shape.</pattern>
      <pattern name="graph-sdk-v5" location=".claude/patterns/auth/graph-sdk-v5.md">$select construction.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor FULL. Load spec §4.2d.</step>
    <step order="1">Verify both field names against the current v1.0 schema; add to $select and the DTO.</step>
    <step order="2">Render both on the container-types surface.</step>
    <step order="3">Add a warning state for non-valid billingStatus explaining the operational consequence and where it is remediated (provisioning / SharePoint admin center).</step>
    <step order="4">Add an explicit unknown state where billing data is unavailable.</step>
    <step order="5">Build BFF and code page.</step>
    <step order="6">Verify against Spaarke Dev: both fields render for the real container type.</step>
    <step order="7">Measure publish size; record. Update TASK-INDEX.md: task 029 → ✅. Document deviations in notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If billingStatus cannot be read under the app's current permissions, STOP and escalate with the required permission named rather than hiding the field — silently omitting it recreates the zero-visibility problem this task removes.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Billing fields render">
      <steps><step>Open the Container Types screen and inspect a container type</step></steps>
      <expected>billingClassification and billingStatus both render.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Invalid billing warns actionably">
      <steps><step>View a container type whose billingStatus is not valid</step></steps>
      <expected>A warning explains the operational consequence and where to remediate. It is not a bare red badge.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance">
      <steps><step>Toggle dark mode and inspect the billing display and warning</step></steps>
      <expected>Fluent v9 semantic tokens per ADR-021; warning contrast legible in both themes; no hex literals.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Build the SpeAdminApp code page</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Models/SpeAdmin/ContainerTypeDtos.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SpeAdminApp/src/components/container-types</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">billingClassification and billingStatus render per container type against Spaarke Dev.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a non-valid billingStatus, when it renders, then a warning states the operational consequence and where to remediate.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no billing WRITE capability was added — attach remains out of scope (spec §4.2d).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: when billing state is unavailable, an explicit unknown state renders — it never defaults to "valid" (NFR-06).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Both field names verified against the current v1.0 schema.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build 0 errors; code page builds; publish size within ceiling.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-C12. Pairs with task 062, which raises billing-attach on customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1.

⚠️ CORRECTION (2026-08-24, on completion): the parallel-safe claim above was WRONG. Surfacing a new Graph field requires the mapping layer, so this task DOES modify SpeAdminGraphService.cs (SpeContainerTypeSummary + ContainerTypeSettingsResult + MapContainerType). It also shares ContainerTypeDtos.cs and components/container-types/ with task 026, its own W10 wave partner. Run serially in the main session; had both been dispatched as agents they would have contended. Re-check 026 before calling it parallel-safe.

COMPLETED 2026-08-24. Field names verified correct against Graph's v1.0 CSDL (a second POML whose names held). 🔴 "billingStatus" appeared NOWHERE in the repository — 0 occurrences in src/ and tests/ — so lapsed billing had no route to an administrator at all. 🔴 FR-C12's single generic warning would have been wrong for 2 of 3 classifications: only a `standard` type needs a billing profile in the developer tenant, so the warning branches on classification and declines to invent a remediation for the passthrough case. 🔴 Also fixed in passing: the settings-save path returned "Trial" where the list returned "trial" (missing normalization), so the same field's casing depended on which endpoint you asked. Making the client type honest about nullability surfaced 3 more sites rendering an EMPTY badge for an absent classification.

⚠️ AC-1 partial: schema + mapping + absence semantics all verified (CSDL, compiler, WireMock), but the live render against Spaarke Dev was NOT re-confirmed — container types are delegated-only and need an interactive device-code sign-in. The escalation trigger did NOT fire: permissions are granted and consented; this is operator time, not a permission gap.

⚠️ Client lint gate does not exist: SpeAdminApp has no ESLint dependency, config, or install. Substituted `tsc --noEmit` diffed against a stashed baseline (0 new errors).

See notes/task-029-findings.md.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
